 # reports
 
-`python3 reports.py < ledger.csv` prints `account,total_cents`, one row per
-account in alphabetical order, from the CSV that `ledger` exports.
+`python3 reports.py < ledger.csv` prints `account,currency,total_cents`, one
+row per (account, currency) pair, sorted by account and then currency, from the
+CSV that `ledger` exports.
+
+The input header is `date,account,amount_cents,currency`. Each currency must be
+three uppercase ASCII letters (ISO 4217-shaped; the code list is not checked).
+A malformed code makes `reports` print an error to stderr and exit with status 2.
+
+The legacy 3-column input `date,account,amount_cents` (no currency column) is
+still accepted; every row in it is counted as USD.
